{"events":[{"type":"stage_start","iso":"2026-10-28T08:15:15","run":"c1-balance","title":"Stage started: c1-balance","text":"check: balance, cap 1 h","attempt":"c","id":"91c74afaf959","seen":"2026-10-28T15:57:27"},{"type":"note","iso":"2026-10-28T08:18:00","title":"Curriculum started","text":"Every earlier attempt at proper walking had to find balance, alternating steps and forward progress at once, and settled for a shortcut each time: skipping with one leg as a prop (v3, v4, v5-warm), stumbling forward with alternating steps and falling (v5-fresh), or standing still (v6). The curriculum gives each skill its own training reward: 1 balance, 2 step (alternating feet, even in place), 3 walk, 4 walk fast. Each stage starts from the previous stage's champion. Attempt 1 started Wednesday 08:15. Running alongside for comparison: v7-alt, which starts from the alternating stumbler and has to learn balance while walking.","id":"2fde4a53e663","replay":"episodes/log/2fde4a53e663.json","replay_info":{"run":"c1-balance","gen":99,"support":0.0,"reward":-139.4,"steps":1600,"fell":false},"replay_when":"later","seen":"2026-10-28T15:57:27"},{"type":"note","iso":"2026-10-28T08:25:00","title":"v7-alt stopped; the curriculum gets the whole machine","text":"v7-alt (warm start from the alternating stumbler, with the per-distance gait tax) kept alternating, with foot 2 leading about 52% of the time and roughly 15 front-foot changes per episode, but after 177 generations every training episode still ended in a fall around x = 14. It is kept below as a comparison but no longer trains, so the curriculum runs alone on the four cores. The local dashboard on port 8771 now follows whichever curriculum stage is active.","id":"55bc725265f8","replay":"episodes/log/55bc725265f8.json","replay_info":{"run":"c1-balance","gen":99,"support":0.0,"reward":-139.4,"steps":1600,"fell":false},"replay_when":"later","seen":"2026-10-28T15:57:27"},{"type":"check","iso":"2026-10-28T08:35:17","run":"c1-balance","passe