 against almost none, 2 falls against 7, but about 10 points lower (260 vs 270), because alternating steps cost more motor effort. The walk-fast stage keeps training to make it faster and cheaper.","id":"01ef68c10045","replay":"episodes/log/01ef68c10045.json","replay_info":{"run":"f5-fast","gen":209,"support":0.0,"reward":272.8,"steps":1035,"fell":false},"replay_when":"later","seen":"2026-10-28T15:57:27"},{"type":"champion","iso":"2026-10-28T15:57:27","run":"f5-fast","attempt":"f","gen":209,"metrics":{"mean":275.7677434142794,"selection":272.22065301088713,"falls":0,"front2_share":0.5353337489407222,"lead_changes":113.2,"abs_lead_mean":0.025210878202221614,"mean_x":88.71244812011719},"title":"New champion in f5-fast: generation 209","id":"641a8f8ebca8","replay":"episodes/log/641a8f8ebca8.json","replay_info":{"run":"f5-fast","gen":209,"support":0.0,"reward":272.8,"steps":1035,"fell":false},"replay_when":"now","seen":"2026-10-28T15:57:27"},{"type":"goal","iso":"2026-10-28T15:59:47","run":"f5-fast","gen":209,"metrics":{"run":"/home/jonas/code/games/bi-pedal/bipedal-CMA-ES/runs/f5-fast","champion_gen":209,"score":264.8923729607809,"x":86.82115249633789,"falls":1,"lead_changes":108.85,"lopsided":0.07083056658900833,"effort":84.97205554611816,"steps":966.05,"checks":{"alternates":true,"far":true,"safe":true,"fast":true},"met":true},"title":"Goal check MET: f5-fast","id":"ed8ee9bd308d","replay":"episodes/log/ed8ee9bd308d.json","replay_info":{"run":"f5-fast","gen":209,"support":0.0,"reward":272.8,"steps":1035,"fell":false},"replay_when":"now","seen":"2026-10-28T15:59:47"},{"type":"note","iso":"2026-10-28T16:06:00","title":"Still improving: attempt 5 polishes the walker","text":"The walk-fast stage of attempt 4 keeps improving, but slowly: its held-out champion went from 267 to 276 over about an hour, with no falls and the feet sharing the lead about fifty-fifty, while its search is narrowing (\u03c3 0.015). The plateau rule will probably end it soon. Its main weakness is effort: about 99 points of motor effort per run, against 75 for the old skipper, which is why the skipper still scores about ten points more. Attempt 5 starts from this champion and makes effort count one and a half times in training, with the real fall cost and the same gait tax, a smaller step size and a larger population for fine-tuning. Both run side by side.","id":"e2e9fa2b5efc","replay":"episodes/log/e2e9fa2b5efc.json","replay_info":{"run":"f5-fast","gen":209,"support":0.0,"reward":272.8,"steps":1035,"fell":false},"replay_when":"now","seen":"2026-10-28T16:07:46"},{"type":"stage_start","iso":"2026-10-28T16:06:36","run":"g1-fast","title":"Stage started: g1-fast","text":"check: none at support 0, cap 10 h","attempt":"g","id":"edfd6a3b0ce4","seen":"2026-10-28T16:07:46"},{"type":"note","iso":"2026-10-28T16:15:00","title":"Check-in: both runs progressing, nothing changed","text":"Attempt 4's walk-fast champion holds at 275.8 on the held-out tracks with no falls and the feet sharing the lead (foot 2 in front 54% of the time); it gained 7.4 points over the last 200 generations, just above the plateau threshold of 5, and its step size keeps shrinking (\u03c3 0.012). Attempt 5 (effort counts 1.5 times) started eight minutes ago and is still at generation 8, so it's too early to judge. No changes, no new podcast episode yet.","id":"5fe427e8b994","replay":null,"replay_info":null,"replay_when":"now","seen":"2026-10-28T16:15:10"},{"type":"goal","iso":"2026-10-28T16:29:52","run":"g1-fast","gen":19,"metrics":{"run":"/home/jonas/code/games/bi-pedal/bipedal-CMA-ES/runs/g1-fast","champion_gen":19,"score":267.9799273842982,"x":88.69923133850098,"falls":0,"lead_changes":119.6,"lopsided":0.12101675978368853,"effort":95.02360746083465,"steps":1107.3,"checks":{"alternates":true,"far":true,"safe":true,"fast":true},"met":true},"title":"Goal check MET: g1-fast","id":"176cbca04bc5","replay":"episodes/log/176cbca04bc5.json","replay_info":{"run":"g1-fast","gen":19,"support":0.0,"reward":268.2,"steps":1104,"fell":false},"replay_when":"now","seen":"2026-10-28T16:29:52"},{"type":"champion","iso":"2026-10-28T16:29:52","run":"g1-fast","attempt":"g","gen":19,"metrics":{"mean":268.0401140748633,"selection":262.12652553734154,"falls":0,"front2_share":0.5619956569302409,"lead_changes":117.55,"abs_lead_mean":0.037486752529527476,"mean_x":88.71100311279297},"title":"New champion in g1-fast: generation 19","id":"428ca2986d98","replay":"episodes/log/428ca2986d98.json","replay_info":{"run":"g1-fast","gen":19,"support":0.0,"reward":268.2,"steps":1104,"fell":false},"replay_when":"now","seen":"2026-10-28T16:29:52"},{"type":"note","iso":"2026-10-28T16:38:00","title":"Model changes allowed: a wider network is queued (attempt 6)","text":"You gave me freedom to change the model itself. The first change: more capacity. The shared leg controller has only 32 hidden neurons. Attempt 6 widens the current champion to 64 using the Net2Net trick: the new neurons start with zero outgoing weights, so the wider network walks exactly like the original (checked: same 272.79 on the replay track), and evolution then learns how to use the extra neurons. Only the size changes, so it can be compared fairly with attempt 5 (extra effort cost). It starts automatically when attempt 4's walk-fast stage ends. Other model changes I can try next: two hidden layers, a memory (recurrent) layer, or repeating each action for two steps.","id":"146aa1de675f","replay":"episodes/log/146aa1de675f.json","replay_info":{"run":"g1-fast","gen":19,"support":0.0,"reward":268.2,"steps":1104,"fell":false},"replay_when":"now","seen":"2026-10-28T16:38:30"},{"type":"goal","iso":"2026-10-28T16:45:46","run":"f5-fast","gen":339,"metrics":{"run":"/home/jonas/code/games/bi-pedal/bipedal-CMA-ES/runs/f5-fast","champion_gen":339,"score":260.80146903439993,"x":86.61275501251221,"falls":2,"lead_changes":112.6,"lopsided":0.08314093718291371,"effort":82.76570188694652,"steps":953.65,"checks":{"alternates":true,"far":true,"safe":tr